19 Be it enacted by the Legislature of the state of Utah:
20 Section 1. Section 1 is enacted to read:
21 63G-6a-111.1. Requirements for landscape maintenance equipment.
22 (1) As used in this section:
23 (a) "Electric-powered" means operated using electricity as the primary power source.
24 (b)
(i) "Landscape maintenance" means routine care of outdoor vegetation and associated elements,
including mulch, gravel, flower beds, and decorative barriers.
26 (ii) "Landscape maintenance" includes mowing, edging, trimming, fertilizing, raking, and blowing.
28 (c) "Landscape maintenance equipment" means any device that is primarily designed for the
performance of landscape maintenance.
30 (d) "State agency" means any unit of state government, including a department, division, office, or
institution of higher {eduction} education.
32 (e) "State government facility" means a building, structure, or other improvement that is constructed on
property owned by the state or a state agency.
34 (f) "State government grounds" means {means } the real property, whether fenced or unfenced, on
which a state government facility is located.
36 (2) Subject to Subsection (3), when a procurement unit procures new landscape maintenance equipment
to replace end-of-life, gasoline-powered landscape maintenance equipment to be used primarily on
state government grounds, the procurement unit shall procure landscape maintenance equipment that
is electric-powered if the state government grounds:
40 (a) are located in a county of the first or second class, as classified under Section 17-60-104; and
42 (b) consist of fewer than 50,000 square feet of property needing landscape maintenance.
43 (3) The director of the Division of Facilities Construction and Management created in Section
63A-5b-301 may exempt a procurement unit, or a specific procurement transaction, from the
requirements of Subsection (2) if {the director determines that the landscape features of the state
government grounds make the electric powered version of the landscape maintenance equipment
impractical for} :
48 (a) {accomplishing } using electric-powered landscape maintenance equipment is not practical due
to the {task for which } existing slope, erosion, stoniness, or other features of the landscape
{maintenance } where the equipment is {intended} to be used; or
